From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op crawl room: the crawl's room-to-stand-up check to the
 module

One more wrapped game function in patch 0005's table
(nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; its id in host/hos_coop_crawl.h), for
oot-remake-multiplayer's 0.12.1 downed-move fix (issue 337):
- 31: main+0x301ac50, is there room for the player to stand up (x0 the
  player actor). Its one caller is the crawl's state step
  (ExecutePlayerCrawl, main+0x27d2fb0): in state 4 a true answer gets
  the player up. In open ground it is true at once, so a downed Link's
  crawl ended as soon as it began and he lay still.
The module answers 0 (no room) for its own downed Link only; every
other call runs the game's check. Nothing else changes: the wrap
machinery, the checks (build id, first words) and the hello's bits are
0005's.
---
 host/hos_coop_crawl.h   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 nx2/coop_world_wraps.py |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 host/hos_coop_crawl.h

diff --git a/host/hos_coop_crawl.h b/host/hos_coop_crawl.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0000000
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/hos_coop_crawl.h
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+   The game's crawl's "room to stand up" check, on Hookshot (oot-remake-multiplayer, docs/play-online.md "Down but not
+   out", issue 337 and the 0.12.1 downed-move fix).
+
+   One wrapped game function more in the one wrap table (patch 0005's nx2/coop_world_wraps.py WRAPS; the id is in the
+   one wrap space of hos_coop_world.h). Patch 0046 adds its row and this file (Hookshot's host/hos_coop_crawl.h is the
+   same file). The module's hos_coop_wrap gets it; Hookshot announces it in HOS_COOP_WORLD_HELLO's bits. The row:
+     (31, 0x301ac50, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bfc, 0xa9024ff4, 0x910003fd, 0xd13b03ff)),
+   Plain C. */
+#ifndef HOS_COOP_CRAWL_H
+#define HOS_COOP_CRAWL_H
+
+/* main+0x301ac50: is there room for the player to stand up (x0 the player actor; a shape cast of its standing body).
+   Returns a bool. Its one caller is the crawl's state step (ExecutePlayerCrawl, main+0x27d2fb0; x19 its node): in
+   state 4 (crawling) a true answer goes to state 5, the get-up. In open ground it is true at once, so the game's crawl
+   of a downed Link ended as soon as it began. The module answers 0 (no room) for its own downed Link only: the game's
+   crawl then lasts the down (its clips, its stick movement, its camera); every other call runs the game's check. */
+#define HOS_COOP_WRAP_CRAWL_ROOM 31u
+
+#endif
diff --git a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
+++ b/nx2/coop_world_wraps.py
@@ -68,4 +68,7 @@ WRAPS = (
     (28, 0x2eb1ed0, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bf5, 0xa9024ff4, 0x910003fd, 0x52832e08)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x21; stp x20, x19; mov x29, sp; mov w8, #0x1970
     (29, 0x2eb2a40, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bf5, 0xa9024ff4, 0x910003fd, 0xf9400028)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30; str x21; stp x20, x19; mov x29, sp; ldr x8, [x1]
     (30, 0x2eb26b0, (0x34000341, 0xb9402c08, 0x34000308, 0xd503237f)),  # cbz w1; ldr w8, [x0, #0x2c]; cbz w8; pacibsp
+    # HOS_COOP_WRAP_CRAWL_ROOM (patch 0046): the crawl's room-to-stand-up check (x0 the player actor; returns a
+    # bool). The module answers 0 (no room) for its own downed Link only, so the game's crawl lasts the down
+    (31, 0x301ac50, (0xd503237f, 0xa9bd7bfd, 0xf9000bfc, 0xa9024ff4, 0x910003fd, 0xd13b03ff)),  # pacibsp; stp x29, x30, [sp, #-0x30]!; str x28; stp x20, x19; mov x29, sp; sub sp, sp, #0xec0
 )


